    {
      "id": "2073686102125203963",
      "text": "Can confirm this isn’t hype — I actually did it.\nBuilt my entire app (Vyta, a life OS — habits, money, journaling, workouts) with Claude as my only teammate. No CS degree, no dev team, coming from construction work. It’s live on the App Store right now.\nThe honest part nobody says though: Claude writes the code, but it doesn’t decide WHAT to build, what to cut, or when a feature is just noise. That part stays painfully human. I redesigned my home screen 4 times before understanding this.\nNow that I’ve shipped once and tested the whole cycle — idea, build, App Store review, real users — I’m planning the next apps. First one was the school fee. The next ones are where it gets interesting.",
      "author": {
        "id": "2062784797668167680",
        "name": "Samuele460",
